            <h1>Welcome Captain.</h1>
            <p class="lead">This page is protected under the OIDC provider.</p>
            <img class="lead" src="https://media1.giphy.com/media/v1.Y2lkPTc5MGI3NjExcGEwcWt4Y2ttejRsdDBvajJhaTVrNzRuczAwdGx0OWNodmxxcmNvYiZlcD12MV9pbnRlcm5hbF9naWZfYnlfaWQmY3Q9Zw/FGbeYTiFyLYmQ/200w.webp" class="card-img-top" alt="pirate">
        </main>

        <footer class="mt-auto text-white-50">
            <p>Whatever we have to say in a footer.</p>
        </footer>
    </div>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js" integrity="sha384-YvpcrYf0tY3lHB60NNkmXc5s9fDVZLESaAA55NDzOxhy9GkcIdslK1eN7N6jIeHz" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    </body>
</html>
```

### `compose.yaml`

```yaml
...
  httpd:
    build:
      dockerfile: httpd.Dockerfile
    container_name: httpd_server
    ports:
      - "8081:80"
      - "8082:443"
    volumes:
      - ${PWD}/apache/httpd.conf:/usr/local/apache2/conf/httpd.conf
      - ${PWD}/apache/ssl.conf:/usr/local/apache2/conf/extra/httpd-ssl.conf
      - ${PWD}/apache/index.html:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs/index.html
      - ${PWD}/apache/protected.html:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs/protected.html
      - ${PWD}/mkcert/app/server.crt:/usr/local/apache2/certificates/server.crt
      - ${PWD}/mkcert/app/server.key:/usr/local/apache2/certificates/server.key
...
```

## Testing the entire stack

Now that all the components have been explained, let's install them.

All sources can be found at: [https://github.com/Dawtio/httpd-oidc](https://github.com/Dawtio/httpd-oidc)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Dawtio/httpd-oidc.git

cd http-oidc/

# add at the end of the file: 127.0.0.1 hydra_server
sudo nvim /etc/hosts

# Create certificate and rootCA
docker compose -f compose-mkcert.yaml up

# Install rootCA on your local machine
# (macOS only)
sudo security add-trusted-cert -d -r trustRoot -k /Library/Keychains/System.keychain $(pwd)/mkcert/root/rootCA.pem

# Start stack
docker compose -f compose.yaml up
```

Now, in your favorite browser, go to `https://localhost:8082`:

![HTTPD landing page](/blog/how-to-deploy-an-httpd-server-with-oidc-provider/deploy-httpd-4.png)

Click on `Authenticate Here`:

![Authenticate Here button](/blog/how-to-deploy-an-httpd-server-with-oidc-provider/deploy-httpd-1.png)

You're now redirected to the `hydra-consent` Docker container.

Credentials are the ones displayed on the screen:

- [foo@bar.com](mailto:foo@bar.com) / foobar

Once logged in, you have to consent to sharing claims with the application:

![Hydra consent screen](/blog/how-to-deploy-an-httpd-server-with-oidc-provider/deploy-httpd-2.png)

And finally, after validation, you're redirected to the httpd server on the protected path:

![Protected page](/blog/how-to-deploy-an-httpd-server-with-oidc-provider/deploy-httpd-3.png)
